      "css": ".ds-back{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;min-height:36px;padding:7px 14px;border:1px solid #e1e8e5;border-radius:8px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.5;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;transition:background-color 140ms ease-out,border-color 140ms ease-out;width:36px;padding:8px;margin-right:4px;background:#fff;color:#122521;}.ds-back:hover{background:#f3f7f4;border-color:#a9bfb3;}.ds-back:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #197b53;outline-offset:3px;}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-back{transition:none;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A report document with immediate access to study images.",
    "overview": "This document records the implemented Reporting Viewer surface in `extensions/reporting`, registered through `modes/reporting`. The supplied screenshot (`/tmp/codex-clipboard-t3tgwT.png`) and [reporting brief](.impeccable/reporting-brief.md) establish its white document canvas, pale green-gray controls, fine borders, compact typography, and restrained green action. The descriptive direction above comes directly from that brief.\n\nThese tokens govern Reporting Viewer only. OHIF's dark imaging workspace and the existing observations extension retain their own visual systems. Preserve the visual boundary when switching between images and the report.",
